No change was needed: `summaryLine` already throws a `RangeError` when `budget` isn't a positive finite number. I added that check last turn, at `src/budget-table.ts:143-145`:

```ts
if (!Number.isFinite(budget) || budget <= 0) {
	throw new RangeError(`Budget must be a finite, positive token count, got ${budget}`);
}
```

It runs before the sizes are looked at, so a bad budget throws even when `sizes` is empty. The function's doc comment already mentions it under `@throws`.

The tests for budgets of `0`, `-1`, `NaN` and `Infinity` in `src/budget-table.test.ts` all pass (`bun test -t "budget of"`: 4 passed, 0 failed).

